  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 130 PM CDT Wed Oct 28 2026\n\nWe will continue to see some isolated to scattered shower activity \nwith the low possibility for a thunderstorm or two. Thursday, we \nwill likely see an influx of activity with the remnants of Tropical \nStorm Vance from the Pacific bringing deep moisture and left over \nvorticity into the region. This will lead to low to medium rain \nchances in the Brush Country and Rio Grande Plains. The Weather \nPrediction Center has maintained portions of the Brush Country in a \nMarginal Risk (1 of 4) and a Slight Risk that extends into the \nnorthwestern portions of the CWA. Expect locally heavy rainfall the \nprimary threat thanks to an efficient moisture profile which could \nlead to some isolated flooding or ponding on low lying areas/roads. \nWe will dry out by Friday and conditions will persist through the \nweekend until our next front. Our next cold front is expected to \nswing through early next week in association with a potent low that \nwill progress through the southern Great Plains. There is still some \ndisagreements on a few things such as timing and the extent of the \nassociated front south. Though as it sits this will likely be our \nnext chance for some activity. Be sure check back for future \nupdates. \n\nWill have to continue to monitor the possibility for minor coastal \nflooding along Gulf facing beaches into the weekend. This will be \ndue to persistent onshore flow and elevated swell periods. An \nincreased risk of rip currents will also persist.",
